.TH cal 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
cal \- print a calendar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cal
[\fB\-jy\fR] [[\fImonth\fR] \fIyear\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
With no arguments,
.B cal
prints this month.  With a year, it prints the whole of that year; with
a month and a year, that month.
.PP
The year must be given in full:
.B cal 9 26
is September of the year 26, not of 2026.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-j
Print Julian days, numbered from the first of January.
.TP
.B \-y
Print the current year.
.SH NOTES
The calendar is right back to the changeover: September 1752 is short of
eleven days, as it was in England and her colonies.  Countries that
changed at another time are not catered for.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# cal
# cal 2026
# cal 12 2026
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR date (1),
.BR setdate (1)
